lcc is the literate C compiler.  It is a retargetable compiler that
generates code for Mips, Sparc, and i386 processors.  The source code
for the compiler can be ftp'd from pub/lcc at ftp.cs.princeton.edu.
Complete instructions on building and installing the compiler can be
found in the tar files.  Version 3.2 is the current version.

An lcc X86 backend for linux is now available in
pub/lcc/contrib/linux.tar.gz from ftp.cs.princeton.edu. You must be
using lcc 3.2; this add-on won't work with earlier versions.

