summary: installs kernels and generates lilo.conf
organization: barefoot serpents
keywords: kernel install lilo boot
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.os.linux.announce

I have uploaded my short, simple, and sweet perl scripts to do automatic
installation of kernel images.  I find them pretty useful for managing 
multiple kernel versions on the same machine; it automates an otherwise
repetitive task that gets tiresome.  Basically, to use it, you simply
build your zImage and type 'kinst'; it copies the kernel to your lilo
boot directory (including the version number of the kernel in the filename),
then automatically generates a lilo config file and runs lilo to install
the image.  Much easier than doing it all by hand.

i've uploaded it to both tsx-11 and sunsite as 'kinst-1.0.tar.gz',
though I'm not sure where it will end up.  You can try:

	tsx-11.mit.edu:/pub/linux/sources/usr.bin
	sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/system/Install

todd.

