Version 2.0h of the JAZZ midi sequencer for Linux has been released.

This is the second official release of this impressive MIDI tool for
Unix/X-windows. If you liked version 1.0 you will sure love this one!

Features include:

   - 2 main windows displaying tracks and single midi events
   - Record/Play
   - powerful and easy event editing
   - volume, pan, chorus, reverb, program, name, .. per track
   - trackstatus: mute, solo, play
   - quantize, velocity, notelength, transpose, copy, replicate,
     erase, merge, move, meterchange, ...
   - load/save midi standard files, format 1
   - multiple undo
   - ...

New features in version 2.0h include:

   - Client/server design - allows sequencer and driver to run on different
     machines. Means that sequencer can run on any Unix/X11 box, not just Linux
   - Support for all 317 Roland GS sounds (not only the 128 GM sounds)
   - Mixer window (slider control of volume, pan, chorus, reverb)
   - Supports altering of sounds (cutoff frequency, resonance...), vibrato,
     pitch wheel sensivity, modulation depth
   - GS Reset support
   - FSK tape sync support (if supported by interface card; works with
     the original Roland MPU-IPC/T card)
   - A lot of bug fixes and improvements
   - ...and more...

Authors:

   andreas@avix.rhein-neckar.de (Andreas Voss)
