The acb-40XX boards are late 1980 devices that allow you to run MFM
or RLL disk drives on a SCSI bus. The two problems with using these
old beasts is that you have to low-level the disk with the bridge
board, and you have to fake the INQUIRY command because it was
optional according to the SCSI-I spec and these things don't support it.

This is just an update to the Nov '94 1.1.6x kernel patch for these 
old bridge boards.  The low level format program is still the same.

Here's the LSM.
Paul.

