	This is an announce for the 4th official version of MD, a device
driver that groups several hard disks or partitions into a single block
device, so it is now possible to have files that grow across devices. It
currently supports a linear mode as well as RAID-0 (striping). Please note
that linear and RAID-0 mode have now moved to BETA, but RAID-1 is still VERY
ALPHA.

What's new since 0.19 :
	Some fixes here and there. Preliminary support for RAID-1 is now
included (not complete yet, since it's still lacking of rebuild tools and
error recovery). Some changes in ide and SCSI drivers to make RAID-1
work... Modularized personalities. Some more speed improvement (using early
requests removal, like in ide.c). Corrected the bug that prevented from
compiling the kernel with module versions enabled (thanks to
pstrode@exec.com for reporting). Updated md tools (use literal chunk size
instead of chunk factor).

Thanks to:
	All the fine people that sent me bug reports, success stories and
docs, everybody at P7 for friendship, disks, net access and Guiness (special
thanks to Reumeumeu ze Great and his VBT).

